#: ../../../reference/tools/google/bazeldeps.rst:4
msgid "BazelDeps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../common/experimental_warning.inc:3
msgid ""
"This feature is experimental and subject to breaking changes. See :ref:`the "
"Conan stability<stability>` section for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/google/bazeldeps.rst:8
msgid ""
"The ``BazelDeps`` is the dependencies generator for Bazel. Generates a "
"*<REPOSITORY>/BUILD.bazel* file per dependency, where the *<REPOSITORY>/* "
"folder is the Conan recipe reference name by default, e.g., *mypkg/"
"BUILD.bazel*. Apart from that, it also generates Bazel 6.x compatible file "
"like *dependencies.bzl*, Bazel >= 7.1 compatible files like "
"*conan_deps_module_extension.bzl* and *conan_deps_repo_rules.bzl*, and Bazel "
">= 7.2 / 9.x compatible files like *conan_deps.MODULE.bazel* and "
"*BUILD.rules_cc.bazel* (with explicit ``rules_cc`` ``load()`` statements "
"required by Bazel 9.x). All of them contain the logic to load all your Conan "
"dependencies through your *WORKSPACE* | *MODULE.bazel*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/google/bazeldeps.rst:18
msgid ""
"Since Conan 2.34, the Bazel 6.x support (the *dependencies.bzl* file loaded "
"from a *WORKSPACE*) is deprecated and will be removed in a future release. "
"``BazelDeps`` still generates *dependencies.bzl*, but it now warns about the "
"deprecation when there are dependencies. Use Bazel >= 7.2 and add "
"``include(\"//conan:conan_deps.MODULE.bazel\")`` to your *MODULE.bazel* file "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/google/bazeldeps.rst:23
msgid "The ``BazelDeps`` generator can be used by name in conanfiles:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/google/bazeldeps.rst:25
